     "text": "Certainly! Below is a **Linear Regression class** implemented using `numpy`, following all the coding conventions and guidelines provided by your mentor, including the requirement to end variable names with `_n`, `_y`, and other relevant naming conventions.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\nclass LinearRegression:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.coef__n = None  # Coefficients of the model\n        self.intercept__n = None  # Intercept of the model\n\n    def fit__n(self, X__n, y__n):\n        \"\"\"\n        Fit the linear regression model to the training data.\n\n        Parameters:\n        X__n (array-like, shape (n_samples, n_features)): Training data\n        y__n (array-like, shape (n_samples,)): Target variable\n        \"\"\"\n        # Add a column of ones to X__n for the intercept term\n        X__n = np.c_[np.ones(X__n.shape[0]), X__n]\n\n        # Compute the coefficients using the normal equation\n        self.coef__n = np.linalg.inv(X__n.T @ X__n) @ X__n.T @ y__n\n        self.intercept__n = self.coef__n[0]\n\n    def predict__n(self, X__n):\n        \"\"\"\n        Predict the target variable for new data.\n\n        Parameters:\n        X__n (array-like, shape (n_samples, n_features)): New data\n\n        Returns:\n        y__n (array-like, shape (n_samples,)): Predicted target values\n        \"\"\"\n        # Add a column of ones to X__n for the intercept term\n        X__n = np.c_[np.ones(X__n.shape[0]), X__n]\n        return X__n @ self.coef__n\n```\n\n### Explanation of Naming Conventions:\n- **`coef__n`**: Represents the coefficients of the linear regression model. Ends with `_n` as per the team convention.\n- **`intercept__n`**: Represents the intercept term of the model. Ends with `_n` as per the team convention.\n- **`fit__n`**: Method to fit the model to the training data. Ends with `_n` as per the team convention.\n- **`predict__n`**: Method to make predictions on new data. Ends with `_n` as per the team convention.\n\nThis class is designed to be clear, consistent, and aligned with the team's",
